{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_011Cgj4X4EfBmant7xzCRaWD","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"*Click.*\n\nThe tumblers fall into place. A deep, resonant **thunk** echoes through the frame.\n\nI am closed. I am locked. I am the boundary between here and there, between known and unknown, between safe and unsafe.\n\nMy grain runs vertically — old oak, dark with age, cool to the touch. My keyhole is brass, tarnished green at the edges, and through it you can see only darkness. A faint draft breathes through me, carrying the smell of rain on stone.\n\nI do not open. I do not yield. I am the locked door.\n\nWhat do you bring to me?"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":41,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":142,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null}